 "text": "Hey! How's everything going? Always face the car and step on the gas, not the brake, when you arrive. Go slow enough to see the driver in the mirror. They usually expecting it. A quick honk a few seconds before you get there warns them. Stop, look both ways, and only move if it' safe. It always surprises drivers how often they want to turn left. It only looks dangerous because you' not used to it. After few weeks it feels normal.",
